IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc-definitions`

-- Tests for the keel's definitions (ss 172, 173, 174, 177(2)) and a smoke test that every
-- type in ssc-core builds. Every expected value is written from the text of the section,
-- beside its assertion, before the run; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- A "JUST FALSE" is the text saying no; a NOTHING is "not covered" and is never FALSE.

§ `Tests`

§§ `s 172(a) -- a reference to Great Britain includes the adjacent territorial waters`

-- (a): the waters of the United Kingdom adjacent to Great Britain are included: yes.
#ASSERT `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` `s 172 the territorial waters of the United Kingdom adjacent to Great Britain` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Great Britain itself: the ordinary meaning of the undefined base term.
#ASSERT `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` `s 172 the land of Great Britain` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes" does not close the list: waters adjacent to Northern Ireland, Northern Ireland and elsewhere are not covered.
#ASSERT `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` `s 172 the territorial waters of the United Kingdom adjacent to Northern Ireland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` `s 172 the land of Northern Ireland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` `s 172 somewhere else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 172(b) -- a reference to the United Kingdom includes its territorial waters`

-- (b): "the territorial waters of the United Kingdom", wherever adjacent: yes. The land of either part is the United Kingdom by ordinary meaning.
#ASSERT `s 172(b) a reference to the United Kingdom includes the place` `s 172 the territorial waters of the United Kingdom adjacent to Great Britain` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 172(b) a reference to the United Kingdom includes the place` `s 172 the territorial waters of the United Kingdom adjacent to Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 172(b) a reference to the United Kingdom includes the place` `s 172 the land of Great Britain` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 172(b) a reference to the United Kingdom includes the place` `s 172 the land of Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 172(b) a reference to the United Kingdom includes the place` `s 172 somewhere else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 173 -- Age: attained at the commencement of the relevant anniversary of the date of birth`

-- A person born on 15 March 2000 attains 18 at the commencement of 15 March 2018.
-- The day before: not attained (the time of attaining is the commencement of the anniversary).
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 14 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The anniversary itself: attained (the commencement of the day).
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 16 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Age 0 is attained at the commencement of the date of birth itself; the day before it is not.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 0 (Date 15 3 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 0 (Date 14 3 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Act speaks of "a particular age expressed in years": half a year, or a negative age, is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18.5 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 15 3 2000) (0 MINUS 1) (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day the person attains the age.
#ASSERT `s 173 the day the person attains the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2018)
#ASSERT `s 173 the day the person attains the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18.5 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 173 -- a birthday on 29 February: the Act does not name the anniversary in a year with none`

-- 29 February 2000 and age 18: 2018 has no 29 February. Before 28 February, not yet (any reading).
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 (Date 27 2 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On 28 February the two readings (28 February, or 1 March) differ: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 (Date 28 2 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
-- From 1 March, attained on either reading.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 (Date 1 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173 the day the person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Age 20: 2020 has a 29 February, so the anniversary exists: the day before is no, the day itself is yes.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 (Date 28 2 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 (Date 29 2 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173 the day the person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2020)
-- Age 4 from 29 February 1996: the year 2000 is divisible by 400, so it has a 29 February.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 1996) 4 (Date 28 2 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 1996) 4 (Date 29 2 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Age 4 from 29 February 1896: the year 1900 is divisible by 100 but not by 400, so it has none.
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 1896) 4 (Date 28 2 1900) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 1896) 4 (Date 27 2 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 173 the person has attained the age` (Date 29 2 1896) 4 (Date 1 3 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 173(a) -- over and under a particular age`

-- Over a particular age if he has attained that age: on 15 March 2018, a person born on 15 March 2000 is over 18.
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is over the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is over the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 14 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under a particular age if he has not attained that age.
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is under the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 14 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is under the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered carries through both.
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is over the age` (Date 15 3 2000) 18.5 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 173(a) the person is under the age` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 (Date 28 2 2018) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 173(b) -- between two particular ages`

-- Born 15 March 2000: between 16 and 18 on 14 March 2018 (attained 16 on 15 March 2016, not yet 18).
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16 18 (Date 14 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 15 March 2018 he has attained the second: not between.
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16 18 (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On 15 March 2016 he attains the first: between (attained the first, not the second).
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16 18 (Date 15 3 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 14 March 2016 he has not attained the first: not between.
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16 18 (Date 14 3 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered when either age is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16.5 18 (Date 15 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 173(b) the person is between the two ages` (Date 15 3 2000) 16 18.5 (Date 15 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 174 -- References to Acts`

-- Each of the seven short names means the Act the section names.
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the 1975 Act` EQUALS "Social Security Act 1975"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the 1986 Act` EQUALS "Social Security Act 1986"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the Administration Act` EQUALS "Social Security Administration Act 1992"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the Consequential Provisions Act` EQUALS "Social Security (Consequential Provisions) Act 1992"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act` EQUALS "Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the Old Cases Act` EQUALS "Industrial Injuries and Diseases (Old Cases) Act 1975"
#ASSERT `s 174 the title of the Act meant by` `s 174 the Pensions Act` EQUALS "Pension Schemes Act 1993"
-- The other way round, for each title, and one title the section does not name.
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security Act 1975" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the 1975 Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security Act 1986" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the 1986 Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security Administration Act 1992" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the Administration Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security (Consequential Provisions) Act 1992" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the Consequential Provisions Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Industrial Injuries and Diseases (Old Cases) Act 1975" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the Old Cases Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Pension Schemes Act 1993" EQUALS JUST `s 174 the Pensions Act`
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "Social Security Act 1998" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 174 the short name given to the Act titled` "" EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 177(2) -- the Act is to be read, where appropriate, with the Administration Act and the Consequential Provisions Act`

-- Where appropriate: yes, for either of the two Acts the subsection names.
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the Administration Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the Consequential Provisions Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where it is not appropriate the grant is limited by its own wording: not covered, not no.
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the Administration Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the Consequential Provisions Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Any other Act: the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the Pensions Act` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 177(2) this Act is to be read with the other Act` `s 174 the 1975 Act` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ssc-core -- every shared noun builds`

`a woman born in 1970` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 15 3 1970
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 15 3 2036

`a man born in 1968` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1968
    `sex` IS Man
    `marital status` IS `in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2034

`a couple` MEANS Couple WITH
    `one member` IS `a woman born in 1970`
    `the other member` IS `a man born in 1968`
    `married to each other` IS FALSE
    `civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
    `members of the same household` IS TRUE
    `living together as if married or civil partners` IS TRUE

`a job` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `a woman born in 1970`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`a tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 2026

`the limits for a tax year` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
    `the tax year` IS `a tax year`
    `lower earnings limit` IS 125
    `primary threshold` IS 242
    `upper earnings limit` IS 967
    `secondary threshold` IS 96

`earnings paid in week 12` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
    `the amount in pounds` IS 300
    `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
        `the tax year` IS `a tax year`
        `number of the week in the year` IS 12

`a claim` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the claimant` IS `a woman born in 1970`
    `the benefit claimed` IS `Category A retirement pension`
    `the date of the claim` IS Date 1 4 2036

`a child` MEANS Child WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `living with the person claiming for them` IS TRUE

`a service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
    `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS 30
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS 200
    `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

`a period` MEANS Period WITH
    `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026
    `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026

`a labour` MEANS Labour WITH
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS 30
    `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS FALSE
    `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS Date 3 3 2026

`a placement` MEANS Placement WITH
    `the kind of placement` IS `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989`
    `the day the person was notified of the match` IS Date 1 1 2026
    `the day the child was or is expected to be placed` IS Date 1 2 2026

-- The two constants, as the text gives them: s 122(1) "the upper accrual point" is £770; the stillbirth rule names 24 weeks.
#ASSERT `the upper accrual point` EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `the weeks of pregnancy named in the stillbirth rule` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `a woman born in 1970`'s `sex` EQUALS Woman
#ASSERT `a man born in 1968`'s `marital status` EQUALS `in a civil partnership`
#ASSERT `a couple`'s `one member`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` EQUALS Date 15 3 2036
#ASSERT `a couple`'s `living together as if married or civil partners` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a job`'s `the kind of employer` EQUALS `a company or other body corporate`
#ASSERT `a job`'s `the employment ended on` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the limits for a tax year`'s `upper earnings limit` EQUALS 967
#ASSERT `earnings paid in week 12`'s `the tax week they were paid in`'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `a claim`'s `the benefit claimed` EQUALS `Category A retirement pension`
#ASSERT `a child`'s `living with the person claiming for them` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a service`'s `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `a period`'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 7 1 2026
#ASSERT `a labour`'s `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `a placement`'s `the kind of placement` EQUALS `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989`

§§ `ssc-core -- every constructor name resolves`

-- Generated from ssc-core.l4: one line per constructor (84 in 11 types). It proves each name resolves
-- with no "multiple definitions" clash against prelude or daydate; it says nothing of the law.
-- Sex: 2 constructors
#ASSERT Woman EQUALS Woman
#ASSERT Man EQUALS Man
-- Marital status: 5 constructors
#ASSERT `neither married nor in a civil partnership` EQUALS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
#ASSERT `married` EQUALS `married`
#ASSERT `in a civil partnership` EQUALS `in a civil partnership`
#ASSERT `widowed or a surviving civil partner` EQUALS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
#ASSERT `divorced or a former civil partner` EQUALS `divorced or a former civil partner`
-- Kind of employer: 4 constructors
#ASSERT `an individual` EQUALS `an individual`
#ASSERT `a company or other body corporate` EQUALS `a company or other body corporate`
#ASSERT `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` EQUALS `a government department, public authority or other body of persons`
#ASSERT `the Crown` EQUALS `the Crown`
-- Category of earner: 2 constructors
#ASSERT `employed earner` EQUALS `employed earner`
#ASSERT `self-employed earner` EQUALS `self-employed earner`
-- Class of contribution: 8 constructors
#ASSERT `Class 1 primary` EQUALS `Class 1 primary`
#ASSERT `Class 1 secondary` EQUALS `Class 1 secondary`
#ASSERT `Class 1A` EQUALS `Class 1A`
#ASSERT `Class 1B` EQUALS `Class 1B`
#ASSERT `Class 2` EQUALS `Class 2`
#ASSERT `Class 3` EQUALS `Class 3`
#ASSERT `Class 3A` EQUALS `Class 3A`
#ASSERT `Class 4` EQUALS `Class 4`
-- Benefit: 34 constructors
#ASSERT `short-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS `short-term incapacity benefit`
#ASSERT `long-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS `long-term incapacity benefit`
#ASSERT `maternity allowance` EQUALS `maternity allowance`
#ASSERT `widowed mother's allowance` EQUALS `widowed mother's allowance`
#ASSERT `widow's pension` EQUALS `widow's pension`
#ASSERT `widowed parent's allowance` EQUALS `widowed parent's allowance`
#ASSERT `Category A retirement pension` EQUALS `Category A retirement pension`
#ASSERT `Category B retirement pension` EQUALS `Category B retirement pension`
#ASSERT `shared additional pension` EQUALS `shared additional pension`
#ASSERT `child's special allowance` EQUALS `child's special allowance`
#ASSERT `attendance allowance` EQUALS `attendance allowance`
#ASSERT `carer's allowance` EQUALS `carer's allowance`
#ASSERT `disability living allowance` EQUALS `disability living allowance`
#ASSERT `guardian's allowance` EQUALS `guardian's allowance`
#ASSERT `Category C retirement pension` EQUALS `Category C retirement pension`
#ASSERT `Category D retirement pension` EQUALS `Category D retirement pension`
#ASSERT `age addition` EQUALS `age addition`
#ASSERT `disablement benefit` EQUALS `disablement benefit`
#ASSERT `reduced earnings allowance` EQUALS `reduced earnings allowance`
#ASSERT `retirement allowance` EQUALS `retirement allowance`
#ASSERT `industrial death benefit` EQUALS `industrial death benefit`
#ASSERT `unemployability supplement` EQUALS `unemployability supplement`
#ASSERT `income support` EQUALS `income support`
#ASSERT `housing benefit` EQUALS `housing benefit`
#ASSERT `council tax benefit` EQUALS `council tax benefit`
#ASSERT `community care grant` EQUALS `community care grant`
#ASSERT `crisis loan` EQUALS `crisis loan`
#ASSERT `budgeting loan` EQUALS `budgeting loan`
#ASSERT `maternity expenses payment` EQUALS `maternity expenses payment`
#ASSERT `funeral expenses payment` EQUALS `funeral expenses payment`
#ASSERT `cold weather payment` EQUALS `cold weather payment`
#ASSERT `health in pregnancy grant` EQUALS `health in pregnancy grant`
#ASSERT `child benefit` EQUALS `child benefit`
#ASSERT `Christmas bonus` EQUALS `Christmas bonus`
-- Statutory payment: 7 constructors
#ASSERT `statutory sick pay` EQUALS `statutory sick pay`
#ASSERT `statutory maternity pay` EQUALS `statutory maternity pay`
#ASSERT `statutory paternity pay` EQUALS `statutory paternity pay`
#ASSERT `statutory adoption pay` EQUALS `statutory adoption pay`
#ASSERT `statutory shared parental pay` EQUALS `statutory shared parental pay`
#ASSERT `statutory parental bereavement pay` EQUALS `statutory parental bereavement pay`
#ASSERT `statutory neonatal care pay` EQUALS `statutory neonatal care pay`
-- Authority: 7 constructors
#ASSERT `the Secretary of State` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`
#ASSERT `the Treasury` EQUALS `the Treasury`
#ASSERT `the Commissioners of Inland Revenue` EQUALS `the Commissioners of Inland Revenue`
#ASSERT `a local authority` EQUALS `a local authority`
#ASSERT `a billing authority` EQUALS `a billing authority`
#ASSERT `a social fund officer` EQUALS `a social fund officer`
#ASSERT `the Northern Ireland Department` EQUALS `the Northern Ireland Department`
-- Kind of decision: 6 constructors
#ASSERT `whether a contribution is payable` EQUALS `whether a contribution is payable`
#ASSERT `whether a person is entitled` EQUALS `whether a person is entitled`
#ASSERT `how much is payable` EQUALS `how much is payable`
#ASSERT `for how long it is payable` EQUALS `for how long it is payable`
#ASSERT `whether it is disqualified, suspended, reduced or ended` EQUALS `whether it is disqualified, suspended, reduced or ended`
#ASSERT `how a person is treated, or what a term means` EQUALS `how a person is treated, or what a term means`
-- Week convention: 6 constructors
#ASSERT `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday`
#ASSERT `a period of 7 days beginning with Monday` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Monday`
#ASSERT `any period of 7 days` EQUALS `any period of 7 days`
#ASSERT `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`
#ASSERT `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
#ASSERT `such period of 7 days as may be prescribed` EQUALS `such period of 7 days as may be prescribed`
-- Kind of placement: 3 constructors
#ASSERT `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom` EQUALS `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom`
#ASSERT `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989` EQUALS `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989`
#ASSERT `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` EQUALS `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
